      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-21T23:39:30Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim,tools): exact undercut stock test and the whole lollipop outline\n\nReview findings on PR #2836:\n\n- The undercut stock law sampled the head disc on rings, so a stock\n  corner between samples passed a plunge and a retract (0.267 mm\n  overlap, no warning). Replace the samples with an exact disc-polygon\n  test: the centre is in the stock, or a stock edge is within the head\n  radius. Pinned by\n  a_stock_corner_inside_the_head_between_samples_blocks_the_plunge_and_the_retract.\n- The lollipop profile stopped the ball at flute_len and stepped to the\n  neck, so the preview hid the upper ball (2 mm drawn at Z 8, 4 mm\n  read). Draw the ball united with the neck up to where it narrows to\n  the neck, start the neck step there, and let the drawn-cutter width\n  law accept the undercut head the laws read above the flute top.\n  Pinned by the_drawn_lollipop_is_the_whole_ball_united_with_the_neck.\n\nRefs #1810\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
